---
import SecondaryLayout from '../layouts/SecondaryLayout.astro';
import { WAITLIST_FIELDS } from '../lib/forms';

// Wedge 2 / Guava BI metadata (company_nav_meta_v7.md §4).
const title = 'Guava BI — Decision Intelligence (Closed Beta) | Guava AI';
const description =
  'Guava BI turns operational inventory data into reliable visibility, important signals, and actionable recommendations. Closed beta — join the waitlist.';
---
<SecondaryLayout {title} {description}>
  <div class="relative z-10 pt-[14vh] pb-xl">

      <!-- Hero -->
      <section class="container" data-section="light">
        <div class="content-container">
          
            <div class="max-w-3xl">
              <h1 class="hero-heading text-shadow-title">See your inventory clearly. Act on it with confidence.</h1>
              <p class="text-enhanced text-shadow-body max-w-2xl mb-lg">
                Guava BI — decision intelligence for inventory-driven operations — turns your operational inventory data into reliable visibility, important signals, and actionable recommendations. It's in closed beta today.
              </p>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-sm">
                <a href="/talk-to-guava" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
                <a href="#waitlist" class="btn btn-outline">Join the Guava BI Waitlist</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The problem -->
      <section class="container mt-xl" data-section="light">
        <div class="content-container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          
            <h2 class="section-header">Inventory you can actually trust</h2>
            <p class="text-enhanced mb-md">
              Inventory-driven operations — distribution, wholesale, retail, grocery, pharmacy, multi-location — make daily decisions from data that's scattered across systems, stale by the time it's gathered, or unverified at its source. The result is slow decisions, missed signals, and corrections made after the cost has already landed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-reduced">
              Guava BI starts where the problem is most concrete: turning that data into visibility you can trust, then turning visibility into signals and recommendations you can act on. This is an initial specialization, not a permanent wall — the point is to solve a real, costly problem well.
            </p>
          
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The value chain -->
      <section class="container mt-xl" data-section="dark">
        <div class="content-container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          
            <h2 class="section-header text-white [&::after]:!bg-white">From visibility to recommendations</h2>
            <p class="text-enhanced text-white/85 mb-lg">The product works in three steps, in order:</p>
            <ol class="space-y-sm list-none p-0 mb-lg">
              <li class="text-white/85"><strong class="text-white">Reliable visibility</strong> — your inventory data is ingested, validated, and brought together across product, location, and category.</li>
              <li class="text-white/85"><strong class="text-white">Important signals</strong> — anomalies, risks, and opportunities are surfaced as they appear, not in a retrospective report.</li>
              <li class="text-white/85"><strong class="text-white">Actionable recommendations</strong> — clear next actions, laid out for a person to decide and be accountable for.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="text-reduced text-white/80">
              The core calculations stay deterministic: your metrics, your numbers, computed the same way every time. Where we use AI — for natural-language answers or explanations — we keep it bounded, controlled, and accountable to the underlying data. We never manufacture certainty the data doesn't support.
            </p>
          
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What Guava BI is today -->
      <section class="container mt-xl" data-section="light">
        <div class="content-container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          
            <h2 class="section-header">What Guava BI is today</h2>
            <p class="text-enhanced mb-lg">Guava BI is an early, closed-beta product, and we're direct about what exists now versus what's planned.</p>
            <ul class="space-y-sm list-none p-0 mb-lg">
              <li class="text-reduced"><strong class="text-text">Deterministic operational metrics</strong> — the core numbers, never estimates dressed up as fact.</li>
              <li class="text-reduced"><strong class="text-text">Cross-product, location, and category visibility</strong> — one consistent view of where inventory actually stands.</li>
              <li class="text-reduced"><strong class="text-text">Anomaly, risk, and opportunity detection</strong> — problems and openings surfaced before they become expensive.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-enhanced mb-md"><span class="font-semibold">Roadmap, not a feature list:</span> Visibility &rarr; Detection &rarr; Recommendation &rarr; Approval &rarr; Execution &rarr; Learning.</p>
            <p class="text-reduced">
              That sequence is a direction of travel. It is not a claim that every stage ships today. Execution — if you choose it down the line — will always be approval-based, with a person accountable at the point of action.
            </p>
          
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Join the waitlist -->
      <section id="waitlist" class="container mt-xl" data-section="dark">
        <div class="content-container max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          
            <h2 class="section-header text-white [&::after]:!bg-white">Join the closed-beta waitlist</h2>
            <p class="text-white/85 mb-lg max-w-2xl">
              Admission is limited while we validate the product against real operations. Joining asks only for your role, your inventory function, and the problem you most want solved. There is no payment, no purchase, and no guaranteed seat — we'll reach out if there's a fit.
            </p>
          
          
            <form
              class="max-w-xl bg-background/90 border border-text/10 rounded-lg p-lg"
              id="waitlist-form"
              data-cta="C4"
              data-event-stem="waitlist_form"
              data-confirm="waitlist-confirmation"
              data-confirm-label="Submitted"
              data-event="guava_bi_waitlist_signup"
            >
              {WAITLIST_FIELDS.map((field) => (
                <Fragment>
                  {field.type === 'checkbox' ? (
                    <div class="mb-md">
                      <label class="flex items-start gap-sm text-reduced cursor-pointer">
                        <input
                          type="checkbox"
                          id={field.name}
                          name={field.name}
                          value="yes"
                          required={field.required ?? false}
                          class="mt-1 accent-[var(--color-accent-two)]"
                        />
                        <span>{field.label}</span>
                      </label>
                    </div>
                  ) : field.type === 'select' ? (
                    <div class="mb-md">
                      <label for={field.name} class="form-label">{field.label}</label>
                      <select id={field.name} name={field.name} class="form-input" required={field.required}>
                        <option value="" disabled selected>{field.placeholder}</option>
                        {field.options?.map((option) => (
                          <option value={option.value}>{option.label}</option>
                        ))}
                      </select>
                    </div>
                  ) : (
                    <div class="mb-md">
                      <label for={field.name} class="form-label">{field.label}</label>
                      <input
                        type={field.inputType ?? 'text'}
                        id={field.name}
                        name={field.name}
                        class="form-input"
                        placeholder={field.placeholder}
                        required={field.required}
                        autocomplete={
                          field.name === 'work_email'
                            ? 'email'
                            : field.name === 'full_name'
                              ? 'name'
                              : field.name === 'company'
                                ? 'organization'
                                : undefined
                        }
                      />
                    </div>
                  )}
                </Fragment>
              ))}
              <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary w-full">
                Join the Guava BI Waitlist
              </button>
              <p class="text-xs text-text/70 mt-sm text-center" id="waitlist-confirmation" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
                You're on the closed-beta waitlist. Guava BI is in closed beta — we'll email you if you're selected. We'll never ask for payment here.
              </p>
            </form>
          
          
            <p class="text-reduced text-white/80 mt-lg">
              Not sure if this is the right fit? <a href="/talk-to-guava" class="text-link">Get in Touch &rarr;</a>
            </p>
          
        </div>
      </section>

  </div>
</SecondaryLayout>